    "title": "Pursuit suspects in custody after chase in South L.A. - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Josh DuBose ,\n4 hours ago Two burglary suspects are in custody after a chase through the streets of South Los Angeles Wednesday afternoon.\nOfficials with the Los Angeles Police Department were reportedly surveilling the suspects before initiating a traffic stop in which the driver refused to yield. At one point, police said the driver committed assault with a deadly weapon on a police officer.\nAn LAPD pursuit ended in the arrest of two suspects on Wednesday, July 15 ,2026. (KTLA) An LAPD pursuit ended in the arrest of two suspects on Wednesday, July 15 ,2026. (KTLA) An LAPD pursuit ended in the arrest of two suspects on Wednesday, July 15 ,2026. (KTLA) An LAPD pursuit ended in the arrest of two suspects on Wednesday, July 15 ,2026. (KTLA) An LAPD pursuit ended in the arrest of two suspects on Wednesday, July 15 ,2026. (KTLA) The LAPD pursues an assault suspect on Wednesday, July 15, 2026. (KTLA) While hitting high speeds, the suspect driver was blowing through red lights, weaving in and out of heavy traffic and driving on the wrong side of the road before ultimately slowing the vehicle to a stop and being quickly surrounded by officers with guns drawn.\nThe passengers exited the vehicle first, immediately raised their hands and laid on the ground. The driver then exited and was also taken into custody.\nSky5 was overhead.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KTLA.\n6",
    "summary": "4 hours ago Two burglary suspects are in custody after a chase through the streets of South Los Angeles Wednesday afternoon. Officials with the Los Angeles Police Department were reportedly surveilling the suspects before initiating a traffic stop in which the driver refused to yield. (KTLA) While hitting high speeds, the suspect driver was blowing through red lights, weaving in and out of heavy traffic and driving on the wrong side of the road before ultimately slowing the vehicle to a stop and being quickly surrounded by officers with guns drawn.",
